Harbourline plc is a listed logistics group. Last year it reported net income of €80m and paid total dividends of €20m. Its balance sheet shows net cash of €150m (cash exceeds financial debt).

An activist hedge fund, Crestview Capital, has acquired 6% of the shares. In a public letter to the board, Crestview argues that:
- the company "hoards cash" and should raise its dividend payout ratio to 60% of net income;
- the roles of chair and CEO, currently held by the founder, should be separated;
- two new independent directors proposed by Crestview should join the board.

The board, of which only three of nine members are independent, has rejected the proposals so far. Crestview has announced that it will submit its own resolutions at the next annual general meeting (AGM) and ask other shareholders to vote for them.
